From 9e5a02f4d09aebfffac48dba693a5157c263b741 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:41:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] upkg: install UHC packages by running their script,
 remove them from the script's Copy lines

A UHC row installs through xsystem 'Execute <UP-Term:uhc>/Packages/<n>' with the pkg wrapper (and its Ask) skipped, rc taken from UHCRC.
Remove parses the script's Copy lines, deletes those files and Installed/<n>, and refuses when the parse finds nothing.
uhc:<n> names the UHC package on a clash; Install All and Update All, launch and interactive skip UHC rows.
